swer.\n\nWait, but maybe the problem is that the fog is rolling in from the ocean, so the front of the fog is moving towards the city. So, the entire city is moving? Wait, no. The city is stationary. The fog is moving towards the city. So, the distance the fog needs to cover is 76 miles. If it takes 337 minutes to cover 2 miles, then the time to cover 76 miles is (76/2)*337 = 38*337 = 12,806 minutes. So, that's the answer", "model_answer": 12806.0, "ground_truth": 12806.0, "is_correct": true}
