 popcorn in four intervals with different rates, followed by a residual heat causing additional pops. Here's the breakdown:\n\n1. **First 12 seconds**: 30 kernels pop.\n2. **Next 12 seconds**: \\(3 \\times 30 = 90\\) kernels pop.\n3. **Next 12 seconds**: \\(4 \\times 30 = 120\\) kernels pop.\n4. **Final 12 seconds**: Half of 120 is 60 kernels pop.\n5. **Residual heat**: A quarter of 60 is 15 kernels pop.\n\nAdding all these together:\n\\[\n30 + 90 + 120 + 60 + 15 = 315\n\\]\n\nThus, the total number of pieces of popcorn Valeria has to eat is \\(\\boxed{315}\\).", "model_answer": 315.0, "ground_truth": 315.0, "is_correct": true}
