unces per cube} = 7 \\text{ ounces} \\)\n\nNext, sum the water used for all cubes:\n\\[ 132 \\text{ ounces} + 143 \\text{ ounces} + 7 \\text{ ounces} = 282 \\text{ ounces} \\]\n\nSubtract the total water used from the original amount of water:\n\\[ 342 \\text{ ounces} - 282 \\text{ ounces} = 60 \\text{ ounces} \\]\n\nThus, the number of ounces of water Yuki has left is \\(\\boxed{60}\\).", "model_answer": 60.0, "ground_truth": 60.0, "is_correct": true}
