 = 165 \\text{ ounces}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Small cubes**: \n   \\[\n   15 \\text{ cubes} \\times \\frac{3}{5} \\text{ ounces per cube} = 9 \\text{ ounces}\n   \\]\n\nAdding the total water used:\n\\[\n120 \\text{ ounces} + 165 \\text{ ounces} + 9 \\text{ ounces} = 294 \\text{ ounces}\n\\]\n\nSubtracting the total water used from the original amount:\n\\[\n344 \\text{ ounces} - 294 \\text{ ounces} = 50 \\text{ ounces}\n\\]\n\nThus, the number of ounces of water left is \\(\\boxed{50}\\).", "model_answer": 50.0, "ground_truth": 72.0, "is_correct": false}
