 mistakes detected in the calculations. So the final answer should be 100 ounces.\n\n**Final Answer**\n\\boxed{100}\n</think>\n\n Oliver has 342 ounces of water and wants to make ice cubes. The problem requires calculating how many ounces of water he has left after making 8 giant cubes, 12 medium cubes, and 15 small cubes.\n\n1. **Giant cubes**: Each giant cube uses 13 ounces.\n   \\[\n   8 \\text{ giant cubes} \\times 13 \\text{ ounces per cube} = 104 \\text{ ounces}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Medium cubes**: Each medium cube uses 11 ounces.\n   \\[\n   12 \\text{ medium cubes} \\times 11 \\text{ ounces per cube} = 132 \\text{ ounces}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Small cubes**: Each small cube uses \\(\\frac{2}{5}\\) ounce.\n   \\[\n   15 \\text{ small cubes} \\times \\frac{2}{5} \\text{ ounces per cube} = 6 \\text{ ounces}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Total water used**:\n   \\[\n   104 \\text{ ounces} + 132 \\text{ ounces} + 6 \\text{ ounces} = 242 \\text{ ounces}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Water left**:\n   \\[\n   342 \\text{ ounces} - 242 \\text{ ounces} = 100 \\text{ ounces}\n   \\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{100}\n\\]", "model_answer": 100.0, "ground_truth": 100.0, "is_correct": true}
