k>\n\nAva and Uma have a total of 113 minutes to walk to the bank. They first take 16 minutes to reach the corner where the gym is, and then another 12 minutes to reach the library. \n\nTo find out how much longer they have to get to the bank, we first calculate the total time they have already spent:\n\\[\n16 \\text{ minutes (to gym)} + 12 \\text{ minutes (to library)} = 28 \\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\nSubtracting this from the total time available gives:\n\\[\n113 \\text{ minutes} - 28 \\text{ minutes} = 85 \\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\nThus, they have \\boxed{85} minutes longer to reach the bank without being late.", "model_answer": 85.0, "ground_truth": 85.0, "is_correct": true}
