blem doesn't mention any other stops. It just says they have 84 minutes total. So, the total time allocated is 84 minutes. They have already used up 11 + 43 minutes, so 30 minutes remain. Therefore, the answer is 30 minutes. I think that's correct. Let me just verify once more.\n\nTotal time: 84 minutes.\n\nTime to mall corner: 11 minutes.\n\nTime from mall corner to library: 43 minutes.\n\nTotal used time: 11 + 43 = 54 minutes.\n\nTime remaining: 84 - 54 = 30 minutes.\n\nTherefore, they have 30 minutes left to walk from the library to the cinema. So, the answer is 30 minutes. That seems right. I don't see any other way to interpret the problem. The key is that the total time they have is 84 minutes, and the time already spent is 54 minutes, so the remaining time is 30 minutes. Therefore, the answer is 30 minutes.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThey have \\boxed{30} minutes longer to reach the cinema without being late.\n</think>\n\nThiago and Fatima have a total of 84 minutes allocated to walk to the cinema together. They first take 11 minutes to reach the corner where the mall is, and then another 43 minutes to reach the library. \n\nTo find out how much time they have left to reach the cinema, we subtract the time already spent from the total time allocated:\n\n\\[\n84 - (11 + 43) = 84 - 54 = 30\n\\]\n\nTherefore, they have \\boxed{30} minutes longer to reach the cinema without being late.", "model_answer": 30.0, "ground_truth": 30.0, "is_correct": true}
