ap to make sure. Total time: 97 minutes. Time already spent: 13 + 22 = 35 minutes. Time remaining: 97 - 35 = 62 minutes. Yep, that seems right. I don't see any other factors here. The problem is straightforward subtraction. So, the answer is 62 minutes.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThey have \\boxed{62} minutes left to reach the bank without being late.\n</think>\n\nSophia and Chen have a total of 97 minutes to walk to the bank together. They have already spent 13 minutes to reach the corner where the park is and 22 minutes to reach the gym. \n\nFirst, we calculate the total time they have already spent:\n\\[\n13 \\text{ minutes} + 22 \\text{ minutes} = 35 \\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\nNext, we subtract the time they have already spent from the total time they have to determine how much longer they have to reach the bank:\n\\[\n97 \\text{ minutes} - 35 \\text{ minutes} = 62 \\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\nThus, they have \\boxed{62} minutes left to reach the bank without being late.", "model_answer": 62.0, "ground_truth": 62.0, "is_correct": true}
