er should be 18 minutes. I don't think I missed anything here. The problem seems straightforward. They have a certain amount of time, subtract the time they've already used, and the remaining time is what they have left. Yep, that makes sense. So, 18 minutes is the answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThey have \\boxed{18} minutes left to reach the mall without being late.\n</think>\n\nMateo and Nia have 99 minutes to walk to the mall together. They spent 13 minutes getting to the library corner and 68 minutes getting to the gym. \n\nFirst, we calculate the total time they have already spent:\n\\[\n13 \\text{ minutes} + 68 \\text{ minutes} = 81 \\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\nNext, we subtract the time they have already spent from the total time to find out how much longer they have to reach the mall:\n\\[\n99 \\text{ minutes} - 81 \\text{ minutes} = 18 \\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\nThus, they have \\boxed{18} minutes left to get to the mall without being late.", "model_answer": 18.0, "ground_truth": 18.0, "is_correct": true}
