he mall is part of the 52 minutes. Therefore, subtracting the time already spent (26 + 13 = 39) from the total 52 minutes gives the remaining time (13 minutes) to reach the park.\n\nTherefore, the answer is 13 minutes. So I think that's correct.\n\nBut let me check once more. Let's imagine the timeline:\n\nStart time: 0 minutes.\n\nTime to gym: 26 minutes. So arrive at gym at 26 minutes.\n\nThen, time to mall from gym: 13 minutes. So arrive at mall at 26 + 13 = 39 minutes.\n\nTotal allocated time is 52 minutes. So from start to park is 52 minutes. They have already spent 39 minutes. Therefore, remaining time is 52 - 39 = 13 minutes. So they have 13 minutes left to reach the park. Therefore, the answer is 13 minutes.\n\nYes, that seems correct. So the answer is 13 minutes. Therefore, they have 13 minutes left to get to the park without being late.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThey have \\boxed{13} minutes longer to reach the park without being late.\n</think>\n\nJamal and Nadia have a total of 52 minutes allocated to walk to the park. The first part of their journey takes 26 minutes to reach the corner where the gym is. From the gym to the mall, it takes another 13 minutes. \n\nTo find out how much time they have left to reach the park, we first calculate the total time already spent on their journey:\n\\[\n26 \\text{ minutes (to gym)} + 13 \\text{ minutes (to mall)} = 39 \\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\nSubtracting the time already spent from the total allocated time gives the remaining time to reach the park:\n\\[\n52 \\text{ minutes (total)} - 39 \\text{ minutes (spent)} = 13 \\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\nThus, they have \\boxed{13} minutes longer to get to the park without being late.", "model_answer": 13.0, "ground_truth": 13.0, "is_correct": true}
