8.00\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(16 \\times 6 = 96\\) and \\(16 \\times 0.75 = 12\\), so \\(96 + 12 = 108.00\\).\n\n2. **Cost of 10 pencils:**\n   \\[\n   10 \\times 18.00 = 180.00\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(10 \\times 18 = 180.00\\).\n\n3. **Cost of the bond paper:**\n   \\[\n   1 \\times 15.00 = 15.00\n   \\]\n\n4. **Total expenditure:**\n   \\[\n   108.00 + 180.00 + 15.00 = 303.00\n   \\]\n\nThus, Faisal spent a total of \\(\\boxed{303}\\) yen on everything.", "model_answer": 303.0, "ground_truth": 303.0, "is_correct": true}
