iple of 3? 150 divided by 3 is 50. Wait, 150 divided by 3 is 50. Hmm, not sure.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the problem is in the translation. Let me check the original problem again. \"In a 150-item quiz, 10% of the questions are biology, and the rest are equally divided as literature and history questions. If Isabella is sure to get 40% of the biology questions, and a third of the literature and history questions correctly, how many points is she sure to get?\"\n\nWait, maybe \"the rest are equally divided as literature and history questions\" means that literature and history each get half of the remaining 90%, so 45% each. So, 45% of 150 is 67.5. So, even though it's a decimal, we have to proceed with that. Then, 40% of 15 is 6. A third of 67.5 is 22.5. So, total points: 6 + 22.5 = 28.5. But points are whole numbers. Maybe the problem expects us to round to the nearest whole number? 28.5 would round to 29. But the problem doesn't specify. Alternatively, maybe the problem expects us to use exact fractions. Let's see.\n\nIf literature and history each have 67.5 questions, then a third of each is 67.5 / 3 = 22.5. So, 22.5 * 2 = 45. Then, 45 + 6 = 51. So, 51 points. But 67.5 is 135/2. So, 135/2 divided by 3 is (135/2)*(1/3) = 45/2 = 22.5. So, 22.5 * 2", "model_answer": 2.0, "ground_truth": 51.0, "is_correct": false}
