that's the answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nCarlos has a total of \\boxed{1219} plums.\n</think>\n\nCarlos picks plums over three days: Thursday, Friday, and Saturday. \n\n- On Thursday, he picks 217 plums.\n- On Friday, he picks 351 plums.\n- On Saturday, he picks triple the number of plums he did on Thursday, which is \\(3 \\times 217 = 651\\) plums.\n\nTo find the total number of plums, we add the plums from each day:\n\\[\n217 + 351 + 651\n\\]\n\nFirst, add the plums from Thursday and Friday:\n\\[\n217 + 351 = 568\n\\]\n\nThen, add the plums from Saturday:\n\\[\n568 + 651 = 1219\n\\]\n\nThus, the total number of plums Carlos has is \\(\\boxed{1219}\\).", "model_answer": 1219.0, "ground_truth": 1219.0, "is_correct": true}
