{"dataset": "ds_main", "item_id": 1071, "question": "Viktor watches TV after he finishes his homework every night. On Tuesday and Wednesday, he watched a 3-hour episode of his favorite show each night. On Thursday, he watched a few episodes of a 30-minute show. On Friday, he finished homework early and watched a 3-hour episode and a 30-minute show. On Saturday, he got to stay up late, so he watched two 5-hour episodes. If he watched 22 hours of TV in all, how many 30-minute episodes did he watch on Thursday?", "prompt": "As an expert problem solver, solve step by step the following mathematical questions. Viktor watches TV after he finishes his homework every night. On Tuesday and Wednesday, he watched a 3-hour episode of his favorite show each night. On Thursday, he watched a few episodes of a 30-minute show. On Friday, he finished homework early and watched a 3-hour episode and a 30-minute show. On Saturday, he got to stay up late, so he watched two 5-hour episodes. If he watched 22 hours of TV in all, how many 30-minute episodes did he watch on Thursday?", "model_response": "<think>\nOkay, let's see. Viktor watches TV every night after his homework. We need to figure out how many 30-minute episodes he watched on Thursday. The total hours he spent watching TV are 22 hours. Let me break down each day's watching to calculate the time.\n\nStarting with Tuesday: He watched a 3-hour episode. That's straightforward, 3 hours. So Tuesday is 3 hours.\n\nWednesday: Another 3-hour episode. So that's another 3 hours. Adding those together, Tuesday and Wednesday would be 3 + 3 = 6 hours total.\n\nThursday: He watched a few episodes of a 30-minute show. Let's denote the number of 30-minute episodes as x. Each episode is 30 minutes, so the total time here would be 30x minutes. But we need to convert that into hours for consistency with the other days. Since 30 minutes is 0.5 hours, the total time on Thursday is 0.5x hours.\n\nFriday: He watched a 3-hour episode and a 30-minute episode. So that's 3 hours plus 0.5 hours. Adding those gives 3.5 hours.\n\nSaturday: Two 5-hour episodes. Each is 5 hours, so 5 + 5 = 10 hours.\n\nNow, let's sum up all the hours from each day:\n\nTuesday: 3 hours\n\nWednesday: 3 hours\n\nThursday: 0.5x hours\n\nFriday: 3.5 hours\n\nSaturday: 10 hours\n\nTotal hours: 3 + 3 + 0.5x + 3.5 + 10\n\nLet me add up the known values first:\n\n3 + 3 = 6\n\n6 + 3.5 = 9.5\n\n9.5 + 10 = 19.5\n\nSo total known hours are 19.5 hours. Therefore, the remaining time must be from Thursday's episodes. The total hours Viktor watched is 22, so:\n\n19.5 + 0.5x = 22\n\nNow, solving for x:\n\n0.5x = 22 - 19.5\n\n0.5x = 2.5\n\nMultiply both sides by 2:\n\nx = 5\n\nSo Viktor watched 5 episodes of the 30-minute show on Thursday. Let me double-check the calculations to make sure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nAdding up all the hours:\n\nTuesday: 3\n\nWednesday: 3 (total 6)\n\nThursday: 5 episodes * 0.5 hours = 2.5 hours (total 8.5)\n\nFriday: 3.5 hours (total 12)\n\nSaturday: 10 hours (total 22)\n\nYes, 3 + 3 + 2.5 + 3.5 + 10 = 22. That adds up correctly. So the answer should be 5.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe number of 30-minute episodes Viktor watched on Thursday is \\boxed{5}.\n</think>\n\nViktor watches TV for a total of 22 hours. We need to determine how many 30-minute episodes he watched on Thursday. \n\n- **Tuesday and Wednesday**: Each day he watches a 3-hour episode. \n  - Total hours: \\(3 + 3 = 6\\) hours.\n\n- **Thursday**: He watches a few episodes of a 30-minute show. Let \\(x\\) be the number of 30-minute episodes.\n  - Total hours: \\(0.5x\\) hours.\n\n- **Friday**: He watches a 3-hour episode and a 30-minute episode.\n  - Total hours: \\(3 + 0.5 = 3.5\\) hours.\n\n- **Saturday**: He watches two 5-hour episodes.\n  - Total hours: \\(5 + 5 = 10\\) hours.\n\nSumming up all the hours:\n- Tuesday: 3 hours\n- Wednesday: 3 hours\n- Thursday: \\(0.5x\\) hours\n- Friday: 3.5 hours\n- Saturday: 10 hours\n\nTotal hours: \\(3 + 3 + 0.5x + 3.5 + 10 = 19.5 + 0.5x\\)\n\nGiven the total hours watched is 22:\n\\[\n19.5 + 0.5x = 22\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\(x\\):\n\\[\n0.5x = 22 - 19.5\n\\]\n\\[\n0.5x = 2.5\n\\]\n\\[\nx = 5\n\\]\n\nThe number of 30-minute episodes Viktor watched on Thursday is \\(\\boxed{5}\\).", "model_answer": 5.0, "ground_truth": 5.0, "is_correct": true}
