7=32. Since the original total was x +16, so x +16=32. Then x=16. \n\nYes, that's another way to look at it. So either way, the answer is 16. So Keisha bought 16 forks. \n\nI think that's correct. Let me just verify once more. If she bought 16, her husband gave her 16, so total 32. She used seven, so 32 -7=25. Which matches the problem statement. So yes, 16 is the correct answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nKeisha bought \\boxed{16} forks.\n</think>\n\nKeisha bought a package of forks, and her husband gave her another package of 16 forks. Let \\( x \\) be the number of forks Keisha originally bought. The total number of forks she had after her husband gave her 16 more is \\( x + 16 \\). Keisha used seven forks for sampling, so the remaining number of forks is \\( (x + 16) - 7 \\). According to the problem, this remaining number is 25. \n\nWe set up the equation:\n\\[\n(x + 16) - 7 = 25\n\\]\n\nSimplifying this equation:\n\\[\nx + 9 = 25\n\\]\n\nSubtracting 9 from both sides:\n\\[\nx = 16\n\\]\n\nThus, Keisha bought \\(\\boxed{16}\\) forks.", "model_answer": 16.0, "ground_truth": 16.0, "is_correct": true}
