sed 10 for tasting, and had 26 left. So the equation would be:\n\n(x + 13) - 10 = 26\n\nTherefore, x + 13 - 10 = 26\n\nx + 3 = 26\n\nx = 23\n\nBut this assumes that the existing spoons were zero. But the problem says \"she was out of plastic spoons,\" so maybe she had no spoons at all before buying. So the answer would be 23. But let me check again.\n\nIf Yara had no spoons initially, bought x, then", "model_answer": 23.0, "ground_truth": 23.0, "is_correct": true}
