o total becomes G + 6. Then she uses 8, so subtract 8: G + 6 - 8 = 27. Simplify that: G - 2 = 27. Then G = 27 + 2 = 29. So the original package had 29 spoons. Let me verify.\n\nIf she started with 29, her husband gave 6, so 29 + 6 = 35. Then she used 8, so 35 - 8 = 27. Yep, that matches the problem statement. So the answer should be 29. Wait, but let me make sure I didn't misinterpret the problem. The problem says \"she used eight of the spoons to sample her beef stew.\" So that's 8 used. Then \"Later, when she went to set the table, she had a total of 27 spoons.\" So after using 8, she had 27. So yes, the equation is correct. So original was 29. That seems right.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe number of spoons in the package Gabrielle bought was \\boxed{29}.\n</think>\n\nGabrielle initially had a certain number of spoons, which we denote as \\( G \\). Her husband gave her an additional 6 spoons. She then used 8 spoons for sampling. After using the spoons, she had a total of 27 spoons left. \n\nWe can set up the equation based on the problem statement:\n\\[\nG + 6 - 8 = 27\n\\]\n\nSimplifying the equation:\n\\[\nG - 2 = 27\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\( G \\):\n\\[\nG = 27 + 2 = 29\n\\]\n\nThus, the number of spoons in the package that Gabrielle bought was \\(\\boxed{29}\\).", "model_answer": 29.0, "ground_truth": 29.0, "is_correct": true}
