 \\boxed{24}.\n</think>\n\nAmelia initially bought a package of plates (let the number of plates in this package be \\( P \\)). Her husband then bought a package of 5 new plates and gave them to Amelia. This means Amelia now had \\( P + 5 \\) plates. \n\nWhile making the beef stew, Amelia used 5 plates for sampling. Therefore, the number of plates remaining after this use is \\( P + 5 - 5 \\). When Amelia went to set the table, she had a total of 24 plates. This gives us the equation:\n\n\\[\nP + 5 - 5 = 24\n\\]\n\nSimplifying this equation, we get:\n\n\\[\nP = 24\n\\]\n\nThus, the number of plates in the package that Amelia bought is \\(\\boxed{24}\\).", "model_answer": 24.0, "ground_truth": 24.0, "is_correct": true}
