her 9, so 34. Then she uses 7, so 27. Yep, that's exactly what the problem states. So the answer is 25.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe number of plates in the package Zahra bought is \\boxed{25}.\n</think>\n\nZahra initially bought a package of plates, denoted as \\( X \\). Her husband gave her another package of 9 plates. After receiving the 9 plates, the total number of plates Zahra had was \\( X + 9 \\). Zahra used 7 plates for sampling, leaving her with \\( X + 9 - 7 \\) plates. According to the problem, she had 27 plates left when she set the table. Therefore, we set up the equation:\n\n\\[\nX + 9 - 7 = 27\n\\]\n\nSimplifying this equation:\n\n\\[\nX + 2 = 27\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\( X \\):\n\n\\[\nX = 27 - 2 = 25\n\\]\n\nThus, the number of plates in the package that Zahra bought is \\(\\boxed{25}\\).", "model_answer": 25.0, "ground_truth": 25.0, "is_correct": true}
