tical point. Let me resolve this. Let's take the problem statement: \"a bag of cookies has 150 calories per serving. If a 100 oz bag has 5 servings...\" So the bag of cookies (which is 100 oz) contains 5 servings. Therefore, each serving is 20 oz. Each serving is 150 calories. Therefore, 1 oz is 150 / 20 = 7.5 calories. Therefore, 7.5 calories per ounce. Therefore, 750 calories remaining would be 750 / 7.5 = 100 ounces. But that contradicts the initial calculation where 150 calories per serving divided by 5 servings is 30 calories per serving. Wait, that can't be. There's a mistake here.\n\nWait, no. Wait, 150 calories per serving. If 5 servings are 100 oz, then each serving is 20 oz. So 150 calories per serving. Therefore, 1 oz is 150 / 20 = 7.5 calories. So 7.5 calories per ounce. Therefore, 750 calories remaining would be 750 / 7.5 = 100 ounces. But that contradicts the other way. Wait, but 150 calories per serving divided by 5 servings is 30 calories per serving. So 30 calories per serving. Therefore, 30 calories per ounce. So 30 calories per ounce. Then 750 / 30 = 25 ounces. So which is correct?\n\nWait, this is a contradiction", "model_answer": 25.0, "ground_truth": 100.0, "is_correct": false}
