otal students: 125.\n\nSwimmers: 36% of 125 = 0.36 * 125 = 45. So, 125 - 45 = 80 remaining.\n\nOf these 80, 40% are in robotics or dancers. So, 0.4 * 80 = 32. So, 32 students. Therefore, the answer is 32. So, \\boxed{32}.\n\nBut wait, hold on. Let me check if the problem is in Chinese or another language, but no, the problem is presented in English. So, the translation is accurate. So, \"or part of dancers\" – so, either robotics or dancers. So, 40% of the remaining students. So, 32. So, the answer is 32. Therefore, \\boxed{32}.\n\nBut let me check once more. Suppose that 40% of the remaining students are in either robotics or dancers. So, 40% of 80 is 32. So, 32 students. Therefore, the answer is 32. So, yes, that seems correct.\n\nAlternatively, if the problem had said \"40% of the students are in the robotics club, and 40% are in the dance team,\" then we would have to use the principle of inclusion-exclusion. But since it's \"or,\" it's simply the union, so 40% of the remaining students. Therefore, 32. So, the answer is 32. Therefore, \\boxed{32}.\n\n**Final Answer**\n\\boxed{32}\n</think>\n\nMrs. Garcia's class has 125 students. 36% of the class are swimmers. \n\n1. Calculate the number of swimmers:\n   \\[\n   0.36 \\times 125 = 45\n   \\]\n   Therefore, 45 students are swimmers, leaving \\(125 - 45 = 80\\) students remaining.\n\n2. Calculate the number of students in the robotics club or dance team:\n   \\[\n   0.40 \\times 80 = 32\n   \\]\n\nThus, the number of students leaving early is \\(\\boxed{32}\\).", "model_answer": 32.0, "ground_truth": 77.0, "is_correct": false}
