 dancers: 25% of 56 = 14.\n\nYes, that's correct. So, 14 students are leaving early.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe number of students leaving early is \\boxed{14}.\n</think>\n\nMrs. Garcia's class has 80 students. 30% of the class are swimmers. \n\nFirst, calculate the number of swimmers:\n\\[\n0.30 \\times 80 = 24 \\text{ students}\n\\]\n\nSubtract the number of swimmers from the total number of students to find the remaining students:\n\\[\n80 - 24 = 56 \\text{ students}\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate 25% of the remaining 56 students:\n\\[\n0.25 \\times 56 = 14 \\text{ students}\n\\]\n\nThus, the number of students leaving early is \\boxed{14}.", "model_answer": 14.0, "ground_truth": 38.0, "is_correct": false}
