the problem says \"of the remaining class,\" so it's 30% of the remaining 90, which is 27. So, 27 is correct.\n\nTherefore, the answer is 27. So, the number of students leaving early is 27.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe number of students leaving early is \\boxed{27}.\n</think>\n\nMrs. Garcia's class has 120 students. 25% of the class are swimmers. To find the number of swimmers, we calculate 25% of 120:\n\n\\[\n0.25 \\times 120 = 30\n\\]\n\nSubtracting the number of swimmers from the total class gives:\n\n\\[\n120 - 30 = 90\n\\]\n\nOut of these remaining 90 students, 30% are either choir members or part of the dancers. To find this number, we calculate 30% of 90:\n\n\\[\n0.30 \\times 90 = 27\n\\]\n\nThus, the number of students leaving early is \\boxed{27}.", "model_answer": 27.0, "ground_truth": 57.0, "is_correct": false}
