ng students. So, 20% of 60% is 12% of the total class. So, 12% of 75 is 9. So, same answer.\n\nTherefore, regardless of how I parse it, the answer is 9. So, the number of students leaving early is 9.\n\nBut let me check once more. Let's compute 20% of 45. 45 divided by 5 is 9. So, 20% is 10%, which is 7.5, and 20% is 15% which is 9. So, 7.5 + 9 = 16.5? Wait, no. Wait, 20% of 45 is 9. Because 10% is 4.5, so 20% is 9. So, yes, 9. So, that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, 45 * 0.2 = 9. So, yes. So, 9 students. Therefore, the answer is 9.\n\nBut let me check if there's another interpretation. Suppose that \"Out of the remaining class, 20% of the students are choir members or part of dancers.\" So, maybe the remaining class is 60%, and within that, 20% are choir members, and 20% are dancers. But that would be 40% of the remaining 60%, which is 24% of the total class. But the problem says \"20% of the students are choir members or part of dancers.\" So, that would be 20% of the remaining students. So, 20% of 45 is 9. So, that's the same as before.\n\nAlternatively, if the problem had said \"20% of the students are in the choir and 20% are in the dance team,\" then that would be 40% of the remaining students. But the problem says \"20% of the students are choir members or part of dancers.\" So, combined. So, 20% of the remaining students. So, 9.\n\nTherefore, the answer is 9. So, I think that's correct.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe number of students leaving early is \\boxed{9}.\n</think>\n\nIn Mr. Smith's class of 75 students, 40% are basketball players. To find the number of basketball players:\n\n\\[\n0.40 \\times 75 = 30\n\\]\n\nSubtracting this from the total number of students gives the remaining students:\n\n\\[\n75 - 30 = 45\n\\]\n\nOut of these remaining 45 students, 20% are either choir members or part of the dancers. To find this number:\n\n\\[\n0.2", "model_answer": 0.2, "ground_truth": 39.0, "is_correct": false}
