inus 1370 is 130. So, there are 130 unoccupied beds after 4 weeks.\n\nWait, let me double-check my calculations to make sure I didn't make a mistake. \n\nFirst part: 1/6 of 1500. 1500 divided by 6. 6*250=1500, so yes, that's 250. Correct.\n\nThen, 40 patients per day for 28 days. 40*28. Let's do 40*28. 40*20=800, 40*8=320. 800+320=1120. That's right. So 1120 new beds.\n\nTotal occupied initially: 250. Total occupied after 4 weeks: 250 + 1120 = 1370. Total capacity is 1500. 1500 - 1370 = 130. That seems correct.\n\nHmm, but wait, is there any chance that the admissions are added on top of the existing occupancy? Like, when they admit 40 patients each day, do they just add to the existing number, or do they first fill up the available beds and then take new admissions? But the problem says \"40 patients are admitted into the care facility each day,\" so I think it's just adding 40 each day, regardless of existing occupancy. So even if the beds are occupied, they can still admit more. So, the total occupied would be initial 250 plus 1120. So 1370. Then unoccupied is 1500 - 1370 = 130. That seems right.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the problem is considering that when they admit patients, they first have to free up beds? But the problem doesn't mention anything like that. It just says 40 patients are admitted each day. So, I think the straightforward calculation is correct. So, the answer should be 130 unoccupied beds.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe total number of unoccupied beds after 4 weeks is \\boxed{130}.\n</think>\n\nThe care facility has a capacity of 1500 beds with 1/6 occupied initially. \n\n1. Calculate the initial number of occupied beds:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{6} \\times 1500 = 250 \\text{ beds}\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate the number of patients admitted over 4 weeks (28 days):\n   \\[\n   40 \\text{ patients/day} \\times 28 \\text{ days} = 1120 \\text{ patients}\n   \\]\n\n3. Calculate the total number of occupied beds after 4 weeks:\n   \\[\n   250 \\text{ (initial occupied)} + 1120 \\text{ (new admissions)} = 1370 \\text{ beds}\n   \\]\n\n4. Calculate the number of unoccupied beds:\n   \\[\n   1500 \\text{ (total capacity)} - 1370 \\text{ (occupied beds)} = 130 \\text{ unoccupied beds}\n   \\]\n\nThe total number of unoccupied beds after 4 weeks is \\(\\boxed{130}\\).", "model_answer": 130.0, "ground_truth": 130.0, "is_correct": true}
