are 1500 - 1025 = 475. So, same answer.\n\nTherefore, regardless of whether the admitted patients are placed in new rooms or existing ones, the total number of occupied rooms would be 500 + 25*21 = 1025. Therefore, unoccupied rooms are 475. So, the answer is 475.\n\nWait, but let me check again. If the patients are admitted into the hospital, they need to be placed in rooms. If the hospital only has 1500 rooms, and 500 are already occupied, then each new patient would need a new room. So, each day, 25 new rooms are added. Therefore, over 21 days, 25*21=525 rooms are added. So, total occupied rooms would be 500 + 525 = 1025. Therefore, unoccupied rooms are 1500 - 1025 = 475. So, that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, if the hospital can reuse some of the existing rooms for the new patients, then the number of new rooms needed would be less. But the problem doesn't specify that. So, unless told otherwise, we have to assume that each new patient requires a new room. Therefore, the answer is 475.\n\nTherefore, after 3 weeks, the total number of unoccupied rooms is 475.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe total number of unoccupied rooms after 3 weeks is \\boxed{475}.\n</think>\n\nThe hospital has a capacity of 1500 rooms with 1/3 occupied initially. Calculating the number of occupied rooms:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{3} \\times 1500 = 500 \\text{ rooms}\n\\]\n\nThe number of unoccupied rooms initially is:\n\n\\[\n1500 - 500 = 1000 \\text{ rooms}\n\\]\n\nOver 3 weeks (21 days), 25 patients are admitted each day. Calculating the total number of patients admitted:\n\n\\[\n25 \\times 21 =", "model_answer": 21.0, "ground_truth": 475.0, "is_correct": false}
