r day for 28 days is 560. So, 250+560=810. 1000-810=190. So, 190. That seems correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the problem is considering that the initial 1/4 is occupied, but when patients are admitted, they are assigned to the least occupied rooms, but the problem doesn't specify that. So, we can assume that each admitted patient takes up one room, so 20 rooms per day. So, 20 per day. So, 560 over 28 days. So, 250+560=810. 1000-810=190. So, 190. So, the answer is 190.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the problem is in another way. Let me check the problem again. \"Calculate the total number of unoccupied rooms in the medical center after 4 weeks.\" So, after 4 weeks, which is 28 days. The initial occupancy is 1/4 of 1000, which is 250. Then, each day, 20 patients are admitted. So, each day, 20 rooms are filled. So, over 28 days, 20*28=560 rooms filled. So, total filled rooms: 250+56", "model_answer": 56.0, "ground_truth": 190.0, "is_correct": false}
