</think>\n\nThe care facility has a capacity of 700 rooms with 1/4 occupied initially. Calculating the number of occupied rooms:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{4} \\times 700 = 175 \\text{ rooms}\n\\]\n\nOver 2 weeks (14 days), 35 patients are admitted each day. Calculating the total number of admissions:\n\n\\[\n35 \\times 14 = 490 \\text{ patients}\n\\]\n\nEach patient requires one room, so the number of occupied rooms over 2 weeks is:\n\n\\[\n175 + 490 = 665 \\text{ rooms}\n\\]\n\nThe total number of unoccupied rooms is the total capacity minus the occupied rooms:\n\n\\[\n700 - 665 = 35\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{35}\n\\]", "model_answer": 35.0, "ground_truth": 35.0, "is_correct": true}
