h 30, so 30 - 30 is 0. Then 82 - 14 is 68. So that would be €68.00. \n\nWait, let me verify again. 82.30 minus 14.30. If I subtract the cents first: 30 - 30 is 0. Then subtract the euros: 82 - 14 is 68. So yes, that's correct. So he has €68.00 left. \n\nBut let me check once more to be absolutely sure. Maybe another way. Let's convert both amounts to cents to avoid decimal confusion. €82.30 is 8230 cents. €14.30 is 1430 cents. Subtracting 1430 from 8230 gives 8230 - 1430. Let's compute that. 8230 - 1000 is 7230, then subtract 430 more: 7230 - 430 = 6800 cents. Which is €68.00. Yep, same answer. \n\nSo all methods lead to the same result. Therefore, Umar has €68.00 left after buying the nails.\n</think>\n\nUmar wants to buy 55 nails at €0.26 each. First, calculate the total cost:  \n\\[\n55 \\times 0.26 = 14.30\n\\]  \nNext, subtract the total cost from his initial amount of €82.30:  \n\\[\n82.30 - 14.30 = 68.00\n\\]  \n\n**Answer:** Umar has \\boxed{68.00} euros left after buying the nails.", "model_answer": 68.0, "ground_truth": 68.0, "is_correct": true}
