   (Each nut costs ¥0.23, so 48 nuts cost \\(48 \\times 0.23 = ¥11.04\\).)\n\n2. **Subtract the total cost from the initial amount:**\n   \\[\n   56.04 - 11.04 = 45.00\n   \\]\n   (Subtracting ¥11.04 from ¥56.04 leaves him with ¥45.00.)\n\n**Answer:** Wei has \\boxed{45.00} yen left after buying the nuts.", "model_answer": 45.0, "ground_truth": 45.0, "is_correct": true}
