rs:\n   \\[\n   27 \\times 0.68 = 18.36\n   \\]\n   This is calculated by multiplying 27 by 0.68. Converting 0.68 to a fraction, we get:\n   \\[\n   27 \\times \\frac{68}{100} = \\frac{27 \\times 68}{100} = \\frac{1836}{100} = 18.36\n   \\]\n\n2. Subtract the total cost from the amount of money Rania has:\n   \\[\n   88.36 - 18.36 = 70.00\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, Rania has \\boxed{70.00} dollars left after buying the washers.", "model_answer": 70.0, "ground_truth": 70.0, "is_correct": true}
