40, and 58 times 3 is 174. Adding those gives 1,740 + 174 = 1,914. Then divide by 100, which gives 19.14. Okay, so that confirms it. The total cost is €19.14. \n\nNow, subtract that from the amount of money Jasmine has, which is €66.14. So, 66.14 minus 19.14. Let's do that subtraction. \n\n66.14 minus 19.14. Subtract the whole numbers first: 66 minus 19 is 47. Then subtract the decimals: 0.14 minus 0.14 is 0. So, the result is €47.00. \n\nWait, that seems straightforward, but let me verify. If I subtract 19.14 from 66.14, the decimal parts are the same, so they cancel out. 66 minus 19 is indeed 47. So, the remaining money is €47. \n\nBut just to make sure I didn't mix up any numbers. Let me recap:\n\nTotal cost per nail: €0.33. Number of nails: 58. Total cost: 58 * 0.33 = €19.14. Money left: 66.14 - 19.14 = €47.00. \n\nYes, that seems correct. I don't see any errors in the calculations. So, the answer should be €47.\n</think>\n\nJasmine has €66.14 and each nail costs €0.33. To find out how much money she has left after buying 58 nails:\n\n1. Calculate the total cost of the nails:  \n   \\( 58 \\times 0.33 = 19.14 \\) euros.  \n\n2. Subtract the total cost from her initial amount of money:  \n   \\( 66.14 - 19.14 = 47.00 \\) euros.  \n\n**Answer:** Jasmine has \\(\\boxed{47}\\) euros left after buying the nails.", "model_answer": 47.0, "ground_truth": 47.0, "is_correct": true}
