ndre has \\boxed{32.00} dollars left after buying the washers.\n</think>\n\nAndre has $55.03 and wants to buy 47 washers, each costing $0.49. To find out how much money he has left, we first calculate the total cost for the washers.\n\n1. Calculate the total cost for 47 washers:\n   \\[\n   47 \\times 0.49 = 23.03 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n   - Breaking down the multiplication:\n     - \\(47 \\times 0.4 = 18.80\\)\n     - \\(47 \\times 0.09 = 4.23\\)\n     - Adding these results: \\(18.80 + 4.23 = 23.03\\)\n\n2. Subtract the total cost from the amount Andre has:\n   \\[\n   55.03 - 23.03 = 32.00 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n\n3. Verification using cents:\n   - Convert $55.03 to cents: \\(5503\\) cents\n   - Convert $0.49 to cents: \\(49\\) cents\n   - Total cost in cents: \\(47 \\times 49 = 2303\\) cents\n   - Subtract the total cost from Andre's amount in cents: \\(5503 - 2303 = 3200\\) cents\n   - Convert back to dollars: \\(3200\\) cents = $32.00\n\nThus, Andre has \\(\\boxed{32.00}\\) dollars left after buying the washers.", "model_answer": 32.0, "ground_truth": 32.0, "is_correct": true}
