m $84.32, subtracting those gives $72.00. That seems right. Let me check with another method. Let's break down the subtraction:\n\n84.32\n-12.32\n--------\nStart from the rightmost digit: 2 - 2 = 0. Then 3 - 3 = 0. Then 4 - 2 = 2. Then 8 - 1 = 7. So the result is 72.00. Yep, that's correct.\n\nSo Gabriel has $72.00 left after buying the 44 washers. I think that's the answer. Let me just make sure I didn't make any multiplication or subtraction errors. \n\nTotal cost: 44 * 0.28 = 12.32. His money: 84.32. Subtract: 84.32 - 12.32 = 72.00. All steps check out. So the answer should be $72.00.\n</think>\n\nGabriel has $84.32 and needs to buy 44 washers costing $0.28 each. \n\n1. **Total cost for 44 washers**:\n   \\[\n   44 \\times 0.28 = 12.32 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Money left after purchase**:\n   \\[\n   84.32 - 12.32 = 72.00 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n\n**Answer**: Gabriel has \\boxed{72.00} dollars left after buying the washers.", "model_answer": 72.0, "ground_truth": 72.0, "is_correct": true}
