f the selling price. The problem says \"transfer fee that is 11% of the selling price.\" So yes, that's 11% of the property price. So that's correct. So total cost is 320,000 plus 6% plus 11%. So 374,400. Which is $14,400 over her budget. So the answer is $14,400. So she is spending $14,400 more than her budget. Therefore, the total price of the apartment is $14,400 more than her budget. So the answer is 14,400. So boxed, it would be \\boxed{14400}.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe total price of the apartment exceeds Ms. Johnson's budget by \\boxed{14400} dollars.\n</think>\n\nMs. Johnson's budget is $360,000. The property costs $320,000, and there are two fees: a 6% brokerage fee and an 11% transfer fee, both calculated on the property price. \n\n1. **Calculate the brokerage fee:**\n   \\[\n   6\\% \\text{ of } 320,000 = 0.06 \\times 320,000 = 19,200\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the transfer fee:**\n   \\[\n   11\\% \\text{ of } 320,000 = 0.11 \\times 320,000 = 35,200\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the total cost:**\n   \\[\n   320,000 + 19,200 + 35,200 = 374,400\n   \\]\n\n4. **Determine the difference from the budget:**\n   \\[\n   374,400 - 360,000 = 14,400\n   \\]\n\nThe total price of the apartment exceeds Ms. Johnson's budget by \\boxed{14400} dollars.", "model_answer": 14400.0, "ground_truth": 14400.0, "is_correct": true}
