total price of the apartment is $48,000 more than her budget.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe total price of the apartment exceeds Ms. Johnson's budget by \\boxed{48000} dollars.\n</think>\n\nMs. Johnson's budget is $420,000. The property costs $390,000 before any fees. The fees include a 6% brokerage fee and a 14% transfer fee, both calculated on the selling price of $390,000.\n\n1. **Calculating the brokerage fee:**\n   \\[\n   6\\% \\text{ of } \\$390,000 = 0.06 \\times 390,000 = \\$23,400\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculating the transfer fee:**\n   \\[\n   14\\% \\text{ of } \\$390,000 = 0.14 \\times 390,000 = \\$54,600\n   \\]\n\n3. **Adding the fees together:**\n   \\[\n   \\$23,400 + \\$54,600 = \\$78,000\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculating the total cost of the apartment including fees:**\n   \\[\n   \\$390,000 + \\$78,000 = \\$468,000\n   \\]\n\n5. **Determining the difference from Ms. Johnson's budget:**\n   \\[\n   \\$468,000 - \\$420,000 = \\$48,000\n   \\]\n\nThe total price of the apartment exceeds Ms. Johnson's budget by \\boxed{48000} dollars.", "model_answer": 48000.0, "ground_truth": 48000.0, "is_correct": true}
