2000} dollars.\n</think>\n\nDr. Patel's budget for the condo is $440,000. The property costs $400,000. There are additional fees: a 7% brokerage fee and a 14% transfer fee. \n\n1. **Calculating the brokerage fee:**\n   \\[\n   7\\% \\text{ of } \\$400,000 = 0.07 \\times 400,000 = \\$28,000\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculating the transfer fee:**\n   \\[\n   14\\% \\text{ of } \\$400,000 = 0.14 \\times 400,000 = \\$56,000\n   \\]\n\n3. **Total cost including fees:**\n   \\[\n   \\$400,000 + \\$28,000 + \\$56,000 = \\$484,000\n   \\]\n\n4. **Excess cost compared to the budget:**\n   \\[\n   \\$484,000 - \\$440,000 = \\$33,000\n   \\]\n\nThe total price of the condo exceeds Dr. Patel's budget by \\boxed{332000} dollars.", "model_answer": 332000.0, "ground_truth": 44000.0, "is_correct": false}
