is 136,800. So 280,000 - 136,800. Let's subtract 136,800 from 280,000. 280,000 - 136,800. 280,000 minus 100,000 is 180,000. Then subtract 36,800. 180,000 - 36,800. 180,000 - 30,000 = 150,000. 150,000 - 6,800 = 143,200. Yep, same result. So the net proceeds are $143,200.\n\nBut let me check if I added the fees correctly. Transfer fees and brokerage fee each are 3% of 280,000. So 3% is 8,400 each. So 8,400 + 8,400 = 16,800. Then the remaining loan is 120,000. So total deductions: 16,800 + 120,000 = 136,800. Then 280,000 - 136,800 = 143,200. That seems correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the problem is structured differently. Let me read the problem again to make sure I didn't misinterpret.\n\n\"Mr. Jones sold his cottage for $280,000. He paid the transfer fees that amount to 3% of the selling price and also paid a brokerage fee that is 3% of the selling price. If he also paid $120,000 for the remaining loan amount of the cottage, how much is Mr. Jones's net proceeds from selling the cottage?\"\n\nSo, the transfer fees and brokerage fee are both 3% of the selling price. So each is 8,400. Then he paid 120,000 for the remaining loan. So total deductions: 8,400 + 8,400 + 120,000 = 136,800. Then net proceeds: 280,000 - 136,800 = 143,200. That seems correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the remaining loan is after the fees? Wait, the problem says \"he also paid $120,000 for the remaining loan amount of the cottage\". So perhaps the 120,000 is the remaining balance after the fees? Wait, but the wording is a bit ambiguous. Let me check again.\n\nOriginal problem: \"He paid the transfer fees that amount to 3% of the selling price and also paid a brokerage fee that is 3% of the selling price. If he also paid $120,000 for the remaining loan amount of the cottage, how much is Mr. Jones's net proceeds from selling the cottage?\"\n\nSo the structure is: he sold the cottage for $280,000. Then he paid transfer fees (3%) and brokerage fee (3%), each 3% of the selling price. Then, in addition to that, he paid $120,000 for the remaining loan. So the total deductions are the two 3% fees and the $120,000. Therefore, net proceeds would be 280,000 minus (8,400 + 8,400 + 120,000) = 280,00", "model_answer": 28000.0, "ground_truth": 143200.0, "is_correct": false}
