g all three together: 38 + 693 + 1026 = 1757. Therefore, the total cost was $1757. Let me just verify each multiplication again to make sure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nDonuts: 2 dozen * $19 = $38. Correct. Mini cupcakes: 9 dozen * $77. 9*70=630, 9*7=63, total 693. Correct. Mini cheesecakes: 9*114. 10*114=1140, minus 1*114=114, so 1140-114=1026. Correct. Then adding them up: 38 + 693 is 731, plus 1026 is 1757. Yep, that all checks out. I think that's the right total cost.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe total cost was \\boxed{1757} dollars.\n</think>\n\nJasmine bought three types of pastries: donuts, mini cupcakes, and mini cheesecakes. To find the total cost, we calculate the cost for each item and then sum them up.\n\n1. **Donuts**: 2 dozen at $19 per dozen.\n   \\[\n   2 \\times 19 = 38 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Mini cupcakes**: 9 dozen at $77 per dozen.\n   \\[\n   9 \\times 77 = 693 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Mini cheesecakes**: 9 dozen at $114 per dozen.\n   \\[\n   9 \\times 114 = 1026 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n\nAdding these amounts together:\n\\[\n38 + 693 + 1026 = 1757 \\text{ dollars}\n\\]\n\nThe total cost was \\(\\boxed{1757}\\) dollars.", "model_answer": 1757.0, "ground_truth": 1757.0, "is_correct": true}
