Answer**\nThe total cost was \\boxed{812} dollars.\n</think>\n\nUma bought three types of pastries: donuts, mini cupcakes, and mini cheesecakes. To find the total cost, we calculate the cost for each type and then sum them up.\n\n1. **Donuts**: She bought 4 dozen donuts at $12 per dozen.\n   \\[\n   4 \\times 12 = 48 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Mini cupcakes**: She bought 5 dozen mini cupcakes at $85 per dozen.\n   \\[\n   5 \\times 85 = 425 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Mini cheesecakes**: She bought 3 dozen mini cheesecakes at $113 per dozen.\n   \\[\n   3 \\times 113 = 339 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n\nAdding these amounts together gives the total cost:\n\\[\n48 + 425 + 339 = 812 \\text{ dollars}\n\\]\n\nThe total cost was \\(\\boxed{812}\\) dollars.", "model_answer": 812.0, "ground_truth": 812.0, "is_correct": true}
