et me just visualize it again. If each loaf is 6 euros, 6 loaves would be 6*6=36. Each biscuit is 4 euros, so 6 biscuits are 6*4=24. The difference is 36-24=12. Yep, that checks out. I don't see any errors here. So, the answer should be €12.\n</think>\n\nTo determine how much more 6 loaves of sourdough cost than 6 biscuits, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the cost of 6 loaves of sourdough:**\n   \\[\n   6 \\text{ loaves} \\times €6/\\text{loaf} = €36\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the cost of 6 biscuits:**\n   \\[\n   6 \\text{ biscuits} \\times €4/\\text{ biscuit} = €24\n   \\]\n\n3. **Find the difference in cost:**\n   \\[\n   €36 - €24 = €12\n   \\]\n\n**Answer:** The 6 loaves of sourdough cost €12 more than 6 biscuits.  \n\\boxed{12}", "model_answer": 12.0, "ground_truth": 12.0, "is_correct": true}
