orrect? \n\nWait, 30 hours is the total work time. The total time available is 150 hours. So, the ratio is 30/150 = 20%. So, 20% of their day is spent cleaning. \n\nBut if you think of it as time per day, they have 15 hours per day. The total work is 30 hours. So, 30 hours / 15 hours per day = 2 hours per day. So, 2 hours per day is 2/15 of a day, which is approximately 13.33%. \n\nBut this seems contradictory. Wait, but 2 hours per day is 2/15 ≈ 13.33%, but 30 hours total work is 30/150 ≈ 20% of the total time. \n\nWait, but how can the same work be 20% of the total time and 13.33% of the daily time? \n\nWait, no, that can't be. There must be a mistake here. Let me check again. \n\nTotal work time: 1800 minutes. \n\nTotal time available: 150 hours. \n\nSo, 1800 minutes / 150 hours = 12 minutes per hour.", "model_answer": 12.0, "ground_truth": 20.0, "is_correct": false}
