 time in a day.\n\nIf they work 15 hours each day, that's 900 minutes. The total work required is 210 floors * 15 minutes = 3150 minutes. So, over 5 days, they have 5 * 900 = 4500 minutes available. So, the time spent cleaning each day is 3150 / 5 = 630 minutes. Therefore, each day, they spend 630 minutes cleaning. Then, the percentage is (630 / 900) * 100 = 70%. Wait, that's 70%? Wait, 630 divided by 900 is 0.7, so 70%. But that contradicts the other calculation.\n\nWait, now I'm really confused. Let me start over.\n\nTotal floors: 210.\n\nTime per floor: 15 minutes.\n\nTotal time needed: 210 * 15 = 3150 minutes.\n\nTotal time available: 5 days * 15 hours/day * 60 minutes/hour = 5 * 15 * 60 = 4500 minutes.\n\nSo, the total time available is 4500 minutes, and the total time needed is 3150 minutes. Therefore, the time spent cleaning each day is 3150 minutes divided by 5 days = 630 minutes per day. Therefore, the percentage is (630 / 4500) * 100. Wait, no. Wait, the percentage of their day spent cleaning is (time spent cleaning per day) / (total time in a day) * 100. So, time spent cleaning per day is 630 minutes, total time per day is 900 minutes. So, 630 / 900 = 0.7, so 70%. Therefore, 70% of their day is spent cleaning floors.\n\nBut earlier, when I thought about how many floors they can clean per day, I got 60 floors per day, which would take 60*15=900 minutes, which is the total time they have each day. So, that would imply that", "model_answer": 900.0, "ground_truth": 70.0, "is_correct": false}
