ded by 60 is 7 hours. So, 7 hours per day spent cleaning. Then, 7 hours per day divided by 10 hours per day is 0.7, which is 70%. So, that's the same as before.\n\nBut if I convert the total time (35 hours) to percentage of daily work time (10 hours), then 35/10=3.5 hours per day. 3.5/10=35%. But that's different. So, which is correct?\n\nWait, the problem says \"what percentage of their day, on average, is spent cleaning floors?\" So, if they are cleaning 70 floors over 5 days, working 10 hours each day, then on any given day, how much time do they spend cleaning. So, if they have to clean 70 floors in 5 days, that's 14 floors per day. Each floor takes 30 minutes, so 14*30=420 minutes per day. 420 minutes is 7 hours. So, 7 hours per day spent cleaning. Therefore, 7 hours out of 10 hours per day is 70%.\n\nAlternatively, if we consider the total time needed is 35 hours, and they have 50 hours available, but the question is not about efficiency. It's just asking, on average, what percentage of their daily work time is spent cleaning floors. So, if they work 10 hours a day, and during that day, they spend some time cleaning and some time maybe doing other tasks. But the problem states that each floor takes 30 minutes. So, perhaps the 30 minutes per floor is the time required per floor, regardless of the day. So, if they have to clean 70 floors, and they have 5 days, each day working 10 hours, then the time per floor is 30 minutes. So, per day, they need to clean 14 floors. So, 14 floors *30 minutes=420 minutes=7 hours. Therefore, 7 hours per day spent cleaning, which is 70% of 10 hours.\n\nAlternatively, if we think of the total time as 35 hours, and they", "model_answer": 35.0, "ground_truth": 70.0, "is_correct": false}
