pent cleaning over the 3 days, which is 22.5 hours, and then divide by the total time available, which is 45 hours. 22.5 / 45 = 0.5, so 50%. So, same answer.\n\nTherefore, regardless of the approach, the answer is 50%.\n\nBut let me check once more. Maybe I made a mistake in the number of rooms per day. 135 rooms over 3 days is 45 per day. 45 rooms * 10 minutes = 450 minutes. 450 minutes divided by 60 is 7.5 hours. 7.5 hours per day. 7.5 / 15 = 0.5. 0.5 * 100 = 50%. Correct.\n\nAlternatively, if I convert everything to hours first. Total time needed: 135 rooms * 10 minutes = 1350 minutes. 1350 minutes / 60 = 22.5 hours. Total work time: 15 hours/day * 3 days = 45 hours. So, the ratio is 22.5 / 45 = 0.5. 0.5 * 100 = 50%. Same result.\n\nTherefore, the answer is 50%.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe cleaner spends \\boxed{50\\%} of their day on average cleaning rooms.\n</think>\n\nThe cleaner needs to clean 135 rooms, with each room taking 10 minutes. The total time required to clean all rooms is calculated as follows:\n\n1. Total time required to clean 135 rooms:\n   \\[\n   135", "model_answer": 135.0, "ground_truth": 50.0, "is_correct": false}
