e 4 kg is 1/4 off the regular price. So 4 kg would be 22 * 0.75 = 16.50 each. So 4 kg would be 4 * 16.50 = 66. So total cost for 15 + 4 = 19 kg is 15*22 + 66 = 330 + 66 = 396. But she bought 22 kg. So maybe the deal applies again for another 15 kg? Wait, but 15 kg would be 19 kg total. Wait, no. Maybe the problem is that the \"buy 15 kg, get 4 kg 1/4 off\" is a deal that can be applied multiple times. So if she buys 15 kg, she", "model_answer": 15.0, "ground_truth": 423.0, "is_correct": false}
