efore, the amount she paid is for 23 pounds. But the problem says \"Buy 15 pounds at $22 per pound, get 6 pounds 2/3 off.\" So maybe the free 6 2/3 is in addition to the 15. So total is 15 + 6 2/3. But she took 23. So maybe she took 15 paid for, and 8 free. But the problem says \"get 6 pounds 2/3 off.\" Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the problem is that the \"get 6 pounds 2/3 off\" is a discount on the total purchase. So if she buys 15 pounds, the total cost is 15 * $22, and then she gets 6 2/3 pounds off. Wait, that would mean she pays 15*22 - (6 2/3)*22. But that would be a discount on the total. But the problem says \"Buy 15 pounds at $22 per pound, get 6 pounds 2/3 off.\" So maybe the total cost is 15*22, and then 6 2/3 pounds are free. So the amount she pays is only for 15 pounds, and the rest is free. But the problem says \"get 6 pounds 2/3 off.\" So maybe the free pounds are 6 2/3. So total pounds would be 15 + 6 2", "model_answer": 2.0, "ground_truth": 509.0, "is_correct": false}
